ABSTRACT
The QUAD Economy is a 4-bite mint/burn ledger with build-credit supply designed to solve credit theft in the coding community. A QUAD is defined as 4 BITES where PRESERVE=0, CREATE=1, MUTATE=2, REMOVE=3. Unlike traditional currencies, QUADS cannot be bought with money. They can only be earned by proving you built something, cemented with a hash, owner, and timestamp. Future technology will be paid for by QUADS - the only way to buy it is to have QUADS. This creates a skill gate, not a money gate, and ensures advanced technology goes to builders who earned it. Every credit is traceable from creation to spend, creating natural accountability and peace for builders.

